    "measurement_method": "Each response_raw scored 0/1 per dimension via curated regex/keyword lexicons (presence-based lexical proxy for a judgment dimension), calibrated against full-dataset hit-rate checks before scoring the sample. Rates = fraction of sampled responses with >=1 marker hit for that dimension. self_deprecating_qualifier_rate, hedge_marker_rate, and question_tag_rate are the explicit linguistic correlates for insecurity/hedging/social-awkwardness claims; the word-count denominator for hedge rate is exact (OBSERVED), the marker lists themselves are an INFERRED judgment operationalization.",
    "addressee_analysis_note": "Addressee comparison uses last_speaker. Core cast (Monica/Joey/Ross/Phoebe/Rachel) each reach sample n>=15 (the MIN_N_FOR_ADDRESSEE_CLAIM threshold used to gate any addressee-specific claim). 'other_non_core' pools all remaining ~121 minor/one-off speakers together; 'no_addressee_null' covers responses with no identifiable last_speaker.",
    "limitation": "Lexical marker lists have limited recall for dimensions that are usually conveyed structurally/tonally rather than via fixed phrases (e.g. teasing, confrontation, sarcasm-adjacent affect). All rates below should be read as conservative lower bounds on true prevalence, not absolute ceilings.",
    "tag_legend": "OBSERVED = directly counted from data fields (marker hits, word counts). INFERRED = the marker-based dimension itself is a judgment proxy. HYPOTHESIS = broader interpretive claim beyond the counts."
  },
